# Probe scratch space, and any lock a local run writes into this Skill's own
# directory. Neither is an artifact: `.fgc/probe-cache/` is #17's cache,
# `.fgc/probe-evidence/` holds the report a lock cites, and `fgc.lock.json` belongs to
# the *project* being decided, not to the Skill.
#
# The evidence directory is ignored because a probe report is reproducible rather than
# committed, which is the same call #17 makes for its cache. It is content-addressed, so
# re-running the probe re-derives the path from the bytes: a reviewer who wants to check
# a record re-measures and compares the hash, and an unchanged report reproduces the
# cited path exactly.
.fgc/
fgc.lock.json

# Local decision files an Agent writes while working. The recording contract is
# `references/decision-recording.md`; a working file is not a delivered artifact.
*.decision.json

node_modules/
*.log
